qx|A3|st||rh||ah|Board 3 IMPs   -   July 24, 2024|pn|hondo717,vs_bbo,aspiring,Hi Its Me|
md|1SK43HAK7654D32CJ3,SJ9762HT32DAQCQ96,STHQ9DJT87CAKT542,SAQ85HJ8DK9654C87|sv|e|MB|?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Using Bergen Hand Evaluation, this hand technically does not meet the |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=ruleof20,Rule Of 20^*N|CP||FP||at| although I have 11 HCP and 9 cards in the majors. On the other hand, when using Bergen hand Evaluation you deduct one for the Jx in clubs so my hand is worth only 10 points.|
PG| ***** 41 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|But I really like my hand with 2.5 quick tricks and I don't want to open 2@H. So I will cheat a little and open 1@H.|
PG| ***** 42 ***** |


mb|1H|mb|1S|sb|SI like the 1@S overcall.|
PG| ***** 43 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|2C|SB|S|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|North is definitely strong enough to bid 2@C. North has both minors and should not worry too much about missing a diamond fit.|
PG| ***** 44 ***** |


mb|3C|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|3@C is good bid, showing a limit raise in spades. Having said that, there is a system I use when there are 2 cue bids available (as in this board which is rare) and that is, a 2@H cue bid shows a 3-card limit raise while 3@C cue bid shows a 4-card limit raise. |
PG| ***** 45 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I am not saying you should play it. But it is good to know. It doesn't come up that often. Further notice East has |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=lott,Law of Total Tricks^*N|CP||FP||at| protection because 3@S is fine as a contract with a 9-card fit.|
PG| ***** 46 ***** |


mb|3H|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|3S|mb|4H|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I personally think West has a very clear pass of 3@H. West had a very minimum 1@S overcall. In fact, particularly with the bad suit, many players would have passed. Further, there certainly is no reason to bid 3@S, particularly with 3 small hearts. I won't bother with undo because of the 4@H bid which I like.|
PG| ***** 47 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Now let us see why 4@H is such a good bid. Once I bid 3@H, which admittedly is a bit of an overbid, North knows I have 6 (or rarely more) hearts. So North knows we have a fit. |
PG| ***** 48 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Using Bergen Hand Evaluation, North hand is worth 10 HCP, 2 length points, 1 point for the quality (3 honor) club suit, and 2 points for the singleton spade, which is particularly valuable in this auction. So the hand is worth 15, clearly enough to bid 4. So good bidding North.|
PG| ***** 49 ***** |


